        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "frūmentum is built on the stem of fruor, \"to enjoy, to have the use of\" (Lewis & Short), with -mentum, an ending for a thing. fruor is usually traced to Proto-Indo-European bhrug-, \"to make use of\" (EtymDB 2.1)."
            }
          ]
        },
